# Front-end structure

Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite SPA for the animal adoption system.

## Alias

Use `@/` for all `src/` imports (Vite `resolve.alias` + `tsconfig.app.json` `paths`).

```ts
import App from '@/App.vue'
import '@/styles/main.css'
```

Do not use deep relative imports (`../../../`) across `src/`.

## Where to put code

| What | Where | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Page / route | `src/pages/` | `pages/AnimalListPage.vue` |
| Generic UI | `src/components/ui/` | `components/ui/AppButton.vue` |
| Domain UI | `src/components/*/` | `components/animals/AnimalCard.vue` |
| Reactive logic | `src/composables/` | `composables/useAnimalFilters.ts` |
| Routes | `src/router/` | `router/index.ts` |
| Styles | `src/styles/` | `styles/main.css` |
| Unit tests | `src/**/__tests__/` | `src/__tests__/App.spec.ts` |

Create a folder when the first file needs it. Do not add empty directories.

## Styles

```
src/styles/
├── main.css      # Tailwind + daisyUI entry (import this once from main.ts)
├── layout.css    # App shell (html / body / #app)
└── tokens.css    # Optional — custom theme tokens when a brand theme is added
```

- Entry: `src/styles/main.css` — `@import 'tailwindcss';` + `@plugin 'daisyui';`
- Global import: `src/main.ts` → `import '@/styles/main.css'`
- Scoped `@apply`: first line of `<style scoped>` must be `@reference "@/styles/main.css";`
- Keep the default daisyUI `light` / `dark` themes until a brand theme is specified
- Put a custom theme in `tokens.css` (imported from `main.css`), not in components

> See @vue-components-style.mdc for CSS conventions.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Vue components / pages | `PascalCase` | `AnimalCard.vue` |
| Composables | `use*.ts` | `useAnimalFilters.ts` |
| Directories | `kebab-case` | `components/animals/` |

